  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HAY - Influencing and Strengthening the participation of Yanomami Woman</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During the period of 2002-2006 the Yanomami women from the Catrimani Mission region, participated in the meetings of the Organization of Indigenous Women of Roraima. During the meeting the participant women felt the need to promote these discussions closer to their communities, thus organizing annual meetings with women from the 24 communities in the Catrimani Mission region.  These meetings started in 2008 and were the only space where the Yanomami women could share experiences between them. Hutukara supported this activity in 2014, enabling the participation of Yanomami women from other regions of the Yanomami land. In 2015, the project will bring together two groups of Yanomami women that will develop research and alternative income. 

The objective of this project is to strengthen the organisation and political participation of Yanomami women, enabling them to access their rights and share experiences among them.</narrative>
  </description>
